## 2026-11-18 — Premium P32 complete
- Theme cross-fade and silicon sheen per premium §8.8, §8.11. Appearance menu choices go through `switchThemePreference` (`src/ui/theme/theme-transition.ts`). It wraps the store write in `document.startViewTransition()`, cross-fades the root over 280 ms `ease-in-out` (opacity only), and calls `skipTransition()` on a running transition when a second choice arrives. It switches instantly when the API is missing, under reduced motion, when the resolved theme does not change, and for OS-driven changes. CSS transitions are off while the theme attributes change, so no element animates its own colours. New `src/ui/wafer-map/sheen-motion.ts` runs the pointer follow: target `clamp((p − c) / R, −1, 1) × 0.05 D` plus `rotate(dx × 3deg)` on `spring-sheen`, one `transform` write per moving frame, rest on leave. The target holds while the camera moves (drag, pinch, spring, inertia) and re-aims at the last pointer after settle. Landing cards and the hero wafer follow at 0.03 D. Touch, reduced motion, and reduced transparency keep the sheen at rest.
- Verified: typecheck and lint clean, `pnpm test` 367/367 (58 files; new theme-transition and sheen-motion unit and property tests). After a fresh build, the new e2e `theme-sheen-p32` passes 5/5 (A2 view transition and persistence, instant reduced-motion and OS switches, stage follow, freeze and rest, card follow at 0.03 D, and the A39 sheen sweep: median and p95 16.7 ms, 0 long frames). `nav-p16`, `scaffold`, `stage-shadows-p7`, `overlay-states-p8`, `wafer-stage-r6`, `loaded-desktop-p12`, `loaded-responsive-p13`, `landing-p11`, `disc-material-p5`, `magnifier-p23`, `zoom-pan-p30`, and `evidence-ignite-p29` pass. `perf-gate` failed only its known long-frame step (median 16.7 ms, p95 33.3 ms). No snapshot or locale changes.
- Decisions (restrained): on this software-raster sandbox the theme-switch frame itself measures 50–60 ms with or without the view transition, so `theme-sheen-p32` gates only that step's median, and its 0-frames-over-50 ms check is left to P34. The rotate term uses the same clamped dx as the offset.
